note that 'lag' is a term used mainly in analysis of data in time, referring to one thing occurring after another. This 
isn't a lag - it's perhaps more accurately called a shift - or maybe an offset - but shift is probably more common for 
distributions, they shift and scale. | 2011-02-13 10:28:50.0 | Spacedman
