[question_id=881] 答案: Now I understand the data. The race on 1983-07-16 is the British Grand Prix (raceId=460). I need to calculate the race completion rate for each driver. Based on the external knowledge, "time has value" means the driver completed the race (has a time value). Let me compute this.

From the data:
- Total drivers who took part: 29 (all rows)
- Drivers with time value (completed the race): Alain Prost, Nelson Piquet, Patrick Tambay, Nigel Mansell, René Arnoux = 5 drivers

So the completion rate = 5/29 = 17.24%

Let me write the SQL query to get this per driver.

